From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] setupapi, ntoskrnl: CM_Get_Parent, and a device node's registry properties

DYMO Connect pairs its USB printer with the printer's queue through the
Printer-class device: it reads the USB device's hardware IDs with
CM_Get_DevNode_Registry_Property (VID and PID), then takes the Printer-class
device whose CM_Get_Parent is that USB device. Both were stubs; it found no
printer.

ntoskrnl records a device's parent when the PnP manager enumerates it
(DEVPKEY_Device_Parent); CM_Get_Parent answers from it. A device node is now
one per device instance in a process, however many device information sets
hold the device, as on Windows -- programs compare device nodes, and the
parent's must be the one their own enumeration gave. CM_Get_DevNode_Registry_
Property(_Ex) reads a node's property as SetupDiGetDeviceRegistryProperty does
(CM_DRP_x is SPDRP_x + 1). SetupDiOpenDeviceInfo reads the Enum key when a
standard user may not open it for writing.

Test: test/usbprint-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_CMDEVNODEPROP,
SG_MUTANT_CMGETPARENT).
